  "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of $2\\pi :$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of $2\\pi $ to $\\pi $:\n\n- $\\pi +2\\pi =3\\pi \\,\u2713$\n\n- $\\pi +2\\cdot (2\\pi )=5\\pi $\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than $5\\pi .$ So, we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of $2\\pi $ from $\\pi $:\n\n- $\\pi -2\\pi =-\\pi $\n\n- $\\pi -2\\cdot (2\\pi )=-3\\pi \\,\u2713$\n\nOf the given angles, only $3\\pi $ and $-3\\pi $ are coterminal with $\\pi .$\n\nSo the correct answer is II and III only.",
